cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CableXSec in academic work, please cite this software entry with
  the version you used. The journal article that describes the method is under
  review; its reference will be added here when it is published.
title: "CableXSec: Component-resolved local cross-section mechanics of dynamic power cables"
type: software
abstract: >-
  CableXSec is an open-source Python library for the local (cross-section)
  mechanics of dynamic power cables. From a cable definition and a section
  load history it computes the axial, torsional and bending stiffness, the
  hysteretic moment-curvature response of helical armour with frictional slip,
  wire and component stresses, contact pressures and slip, temperatures, and
  fatigue damage at fixed material points of every wire. It reads global
  results of CableDyn, RIFLEX and CSV exports and turns them into fatigue damage
  of the armour, the conductor and the sheaths.
